---
import { Image } from "astro:assets";

import version0image from "#assets/images/lowmess-com_version-0.png";
import version1image from "#assets/images/lowmess-com_version-1.png";
import version2image from "#assets/images/lowmess-com_version-2.png";
import version3image from "#assets/images/lowmess-com_version-3.png";
import version4image from "#assets/images/lowmess-com_version-4.png";
import version5image from "#assets/images/lowmess-com_version-5.png";
import version6image from "#assets/images/lowmess-com_version-6.png";
import NumberedSection from "#components/numbered-section.astro";
import PageHeading from "#components/page-heading.astro";
import SectionHeading from "#components/section-heading.astro";
import ArrowRight from "#icons/arrow-right.svg";
import GlobalLayout from "#layouts/global.astro";
---

<GlobalLayout title="Archive">
	<PageHeading>Visions of websites past</PageHeading>

	<NumberedSection as="article" class="counter-reset">
		<SectionHeading>2014&ndash;2015</SectionHeading>

		<div class="archive-preview">
			<Image src={version0image} alt="" />

			<div>
				<p>
					The code for this version is (perhaps fortunately) lost to time. The
					only thing I remember about it is that it had similar navigation to
					v1. And that it was built as a student project using student design
					work. That&apos;s called efficiency.
				</p>

				<p class="tooling">
					Built with <a href="https://jquery.com/">jQuery</a>, I assume.
				</p>
			</div>
		</div></NumberedSection
	>

	<NumberedSection as="article">
		<SectionHeading>2015&ndash;2017</SectionHeading>

		<div class="archive-preview">
			<Image src={version1image} alt="" />

			<div>
				<p>
					Mostly this was a showcase for the design work I did as a student, but
					if you look closely you can find some client work. The copy (and color
					contrast) on this site is really bad, and I find it&apos;s best to not
					think about the quality of the code.
				</p>

				<p>
					<a href="https://v1.lowmess.com/" class="archive-site"
						>Visit version 1 <ArrowRight /></a
					>
				</p>

				<p class="tooling">
					Built with <a href="https://prepros.io/">Prepros</a>, <a
						href="https://pugjs.org/">Pug (née Jade)</a
					>,{" "}
					<a href="https://sass-lang.com">Sass</a>, and <a
						href="https://jquery.com/">jQuery</a
					>.
				</p>
			</div>
		</div></NumberedSection
	>

	<NumberedSection as="article">
		<SectionHeading>2017</SectionHeading>

		<div class="archive-preview">
			<Image src={version2image} alt="" />

			<div>
				<p>
					The first portfolio I made as a developer. I hated the design on this
					one basically as soon as I launched it, and it lasted fewer than 6
					months before I scrapped it for v3.
				</p>

				<p>
					<a href="https://v2.lowmess.com/" class="archive-site"
						>Visit version 2 <ArrowRight /></a
					>
				</p>

				<p class="tooling">
					Built with <a href="https://rollupjs.org">Rollup</a>, <a
						href="https://metalsmith.io">Metalsmith</a
					>, <a href="https://pugjs.org">Pug</a>, <a href="https://postcss.org"
						>PostCSS</a
					>, and <a href="http://tachyons.io">Tachyons</a>.
				</p>
			</div>
		</div></NumberedSection
	>

	<NumberedSection as="article">
		<SectionHeading>2017&ndash;2020</SectionHeading>

		<div class="archive-preview">
			<Image src={version3image} alt="" />

			<div>
				<p>
					This design proved popular, and several developers forked the repo and
					used it as a basis for their own sites. However it proved limiting
					when I wanted to implement dark mode. Also I got bored of it (the
					Designer&apos;s Curse&trade;).
				</p>

				<p>
					<a href="https://v3.lowmess.com/" class="archive-site"
						>Visit version 3 <ArrowRight /></a
					>
				</p>

				<p class="tooling">
					Built with <a href="https://gatsbyjs.com">Gatsby</a>, <a
						href="https://preactjs.com">Preact</a
					>, <a href="https://mdxjs.com">MDX</a>, and <a
						href="https://rebassjs.org">Rebass</a
					>.
				</p>
			</div>
		</div></NumberedSection
	>

	<NumberedSection as="article">
		<SectionHeading>2020&ndash;2024</SectionHeading>

		<div class="archive-preview">
			<Image src={version4image} alt="" />

			<div>
				<p>
					This design survived a change of framework (<a
						href="/blog/migrate-gatsby-next">Gatsby to Next.js</a
					>). The star of the show was something relegated to the about page in
					v3: a rolling 30-day stat aggregation. Unfortunately, several sites
					restricting API access crippled the homepage.
				</p>

				<p class="links">
					<a href="https://v4.lowmess.com/" class="archive-site"
						>Visit version 4 <ArrowRight /></a
					>
				</p>

				<p class="tooling">
					Built with <a href="https://gatsbyjs.com">Gatsby</a>/<a
						href="https://nextjs.org">Next.js</a
					>, <a href="https://preactjs.com">Preact</a>, <a
						href="https://mdxjs.com">MDX</a
					>, and <a href="https://theme-ui.com">Theme UI</a>.
				</p>
			</div>
		</div></NumberedSection
	>

	<NumberedSection as="article">
		<SectionHeading>2025&ndash;2026</SectionHeading>

		<div class="archive-preview">
			<Image src={version5image} alt="" />

			<div>
				<p>
					As API access became a rare commodity, I needed to pivot. Also I
					wanted to use <a href="https://astro.build/">Astro</a>. You can read
					about some of the design process in <a href="/blog/redesign-2025"
						>this blog post</a
					>.
				</p>

				<p>
					<a href="https://v5.lowmess.com/" class="archive-site"
						>Visit version 5 <ArrowRight /></a
					>
				</p>

				<p class="tooling">
					Built with <a href="https://astro.build">Astro</a> and <a
						href="https://mdxjs.com">MDX</a
					>.
				</p>
			</div>
		</div></NumberedSection
	>

	<NumberedSection as="article">
		<SectionHeading>2026&ndash;</SectionHeading>

		<div class="archive-preview">
			<Image src={version6image} alt="" />

			<div>
				<p>It is this website. You are on it right now.</p>

				<p class="tooling">
					Built with <a href="https://astro.build">Astro</a> and <a
						href="/colophon">some friends</a
					>.
				</p>
			</div>
		</div></NumberedSection
	>
</GlobalLayout>

<style>
	.counter-reset {
		counter-reset: numbered-section -1;
	}

	.title {
		font-size: var(--font-size-lg);
		line-height: var(--line-height-heading);
		font-family: var(--font-family-heading);
		font-weight: 500;
		color: var(--color-text);
	}

	.tooling {
		color: var(--color-text-secondary);
		font-size: var(--font-size-sm);

		a {
			color: inherit;
			text-decoration-color: var(--color-text);

			&:hover {
				color: var(--color-text);
			}
		}
	}

	p {
		margin: 0;
		max-width: 55ch;
		text-wrap: pretty;
	}

	p + p {
		margin-block-start: var(--rhythm-md);
	}

	a {
		color: inherit;
		text-decoration-color: var(--color-primary);

		&:hover {
			color: var(--color-primary);
		}
	}

	.archive-site {
		color: var(--color-text);
		text-decoration: none;

		&:hover {
			color: var(--color-primary);

			svg {
				transform: translateX(var(--space-xs));
			}
		}

		svg {
			width: 1em;
			position: relative;
			top: -2px;
			transition: transform 0.2s ease;
		}
	}

	.archive-preview {
		display: flex;
		flex-direction: column;
		gap: var(--rhythm-md);
		margin-block-start: var(--rhythm-lg);

		img {
			max-width: 360px;
			aspect-ratio: 4 / 3;
			object-fit: cover;
		}

		@media (min-width: 55em) {
			flex-direction: row;
			gap: var(--space-xl);
			align-items: center;
		}
	}

	.links {
		display: flex;
		gap: var(--space-md);
	}

	article {
		break-inside: avoid;
	}
</style>
